ated me and my doctor who was  taking this very seriously held my hand  for the first time since I had gotten  sick and said this is not easy and this  is not straightforward but I'm gonna try  really hard and we're gonna figure this  out for you that moment of this is what  you have you have a name you can write  this down on your paperwork  you can tell this to loved ones we have  a path and maybe it's not super clear  and we're gonna have to switch around  your medications a lot but you have this  thing and you have not been crazy this  whole time it was a stunning moment it  gave me the fuel that I needed to go  forward with treatment for over a year  with intensity I would be throwing up so  much have no appetite and look like  complete [ __ ] and I would just smile so  much because I knew that the medication  that was making me sick was doing  something and that's why I was getting  sick and it was this this whole process  in my brain like a challenge like I was  fighting these bugs that were in my body  having a goal versus just going down and  down and thinking that you're crazy  they're incomparable and it gets easier  the further I get away from my former  self because letting go of her has been  very difficult hearing from doctors and  hearing from loved ones is always  reassuring and getting an answer or  getting support is what we all want but  no one will ever ever ever know what's  going on inside of your body are going  on inside of your brain unless you tell  them and in order to tell them  confidently  you have to have been listening to  yourself anything that seems abnormal to  you listen to it and remind yourself  that you are worth paying attention to  yourself and if you don't understand and  believe yourself no one else will  [Music]
 

